person "==Researcher\n<size:16>[Person]</size>\n\nDesigns waveguides, rings and phononic cells; runs mode and eigenfrequency studies; compares runs." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxQZXJzb24=>> as Researcher
rectangle "==AI host\n<size:16>[Software System]</size>\n\nClaude Code or Claude Desktop (any MCP host). Drives nyx through the engine commands as MCP tools." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxTb2Z0d2FyZSBTeXN0ZW0sRXh0ZXJuYWw=>> as AIhost
rectangle "==Results viewer\n<size:16>[Software System]</size>\n\nParaView or VisIt. Reads the XDMF description and the HDF5 results file." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxTb2Z0d2FyZSBTeXN0ZW0sRXh0ZXJuYWw=>> as Resultsviewer
database "==Workspace folder\n<size:16>[Software System]</size>\n\nDocuments/nyx on disk: workflows, runs, .nyx archives, project files." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxTb2Z0d2FyZSBTeXN0ZW0sRXh0ZXJuYWwsU3RvcmU=>> as Workspacefolder

rectangle "nyx\n<size:16>[Software System]</size>" <<Boundary-bnl4>> {
  component "==geom\n<size:16>[Container: Rust library]</size>\n\nLean CSG-over-B-rep geometry kernel: feature lists, named regions and boundaries, selectors, exact projection oracles. Depends on serde and optional rayon only." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsTGlicmFyeQ==>> as nyx.geom
  database "==Project file\n<size:16>[Container: File .nyx.json]</size>\n\nEverything saved for one model: geometry, materials, boundary conditions, studies. JSON with a format key." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsU3RvcmU=>> as nyx.Projectfile
  database "==Results file\n<size:16>[Container: File .h5 and .xdmf]</size>\n\nProject, mesh and every solution of every solved physics, compressed, exact; with an XDMF description next to it." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsU3RvcmU=>> as nyx.Resultsfile
  database "==Workspace data\n<size:16>[Container: Files and folders]</size>\n\nworkspace.json, workflow.json, history.jsonl, runs.jsonl, specs/ (experiment.nyx.json, specs/<hash>.nyx.json), run folders with results.h5, .nyx archives." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsU3RvcmU=>> as nyx.Workspacedata
  database "==Material library\n<size:16>[Container: Files]</size>\n\nmaterials/*.toml next to the program: silicon, silica, sapphire, metals, nitrides, niobate and more, with sources." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsU3RvcmU=>> as nyx.Materiallibrary
  rectangle "==nyx-mcp\n<size:16>[Container: Rust binary]</size>\n\nThe MCP server (stdio, JSON-RPC 2.0): every tool is one engine command, with the JSON Schema the engine generates." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsRXhlY3V0YWJsZQ==>> as nyx.nyxmcp
  rectangle "==nyx-script\n<size:16>[Container: Rust library and worker binary]</size>\n\nScripts, a third front-end of the engine: Python-syntax text (*.nys) run by Monty in a worker process; each nyx.<command>(...) is one Engine::call. Limits, no ambient access, the engine's path guard." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsRXhlY3V0YWJsZQ==>> as nyx.nyxscript
  rectangle "==nyx-connect\n<size:16>[Container: Rust library and binary]</size>\n\nFinds Claude Code and Claude Desktop installs and registers nyx-mcp with them; the Connect menu and its command-line twin." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsRXhlY3V0YWJsZQ==>> as nyx.nyxconnect
  component "==nyx-engine\n<size:16>[Container: Rust library]</size>\n\nThe Engine: one project, the mesh built for it, the latest result of each physics, the jobs that produce them, and the binding to a workflow. Every action is a named command with a JSON Schema." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsTGlicmFyeQ==>> as nyx.nyxengine
  component "==nyx-physics\n<size:16>[Container: Rust library]</size>\n\nThe Physics trait, the problem envelope (ProblemSpec), descriptors, SolveResult, the registry type, validation, JSON Schemas." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsTGlicmFyeQ==>> as nyx.nyxphysics
  component "==nyx-dfs\n<size:16>[Container: Rust library]</size>\n\nDiffusion physics: heat and electrostatics. Typed problem, three-stage kernels, descriptors, goldens." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsTGlicmFyeSxLZXJuZWw=>> as nyx.nyxdfs
  component "==nyx-sms\n<size:16>[Container: Rust library]</size>\n\nSolid mechanics: static, eigenfrequency, PML, Floquet, low-reflecting boundaries, axisymmetric." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsTGlicmFyeSxLZXJuZWw=>> as nyx.nyxsms
  rectangle "==app\n<size:16>[Container: Rust, eframe/egui]</size>\n\nThe egui window (binary nyx): geometry editor, mesh view, Study, Physics and Materials tabs drawn from the physics descriptors, results, analysis, workflow dashboard. A front-end of the engine: it holds an Engine and calls commands." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsRXhlY3V0YWJsZQ==>> as nyx.app
  component "==nyx-ems\n<size:16>[Container: Rust library]</size>\n\nEM waves: waveguide modes (real and complex), axisymmetric, cavity in 3D." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsTGlicmFyeSxLZXJuZWw=>> as nyx.nyxems
  component "==nyx-analysis\n<size:16>[Container: Rust library]</size>\n\nAnalyses of results: the polarization (Stokes parameters, Poincare sphere, classes, degenerate groups) as a function of a SolveResult and its mesh." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsTGlicmFyeQ==>> as nyx.nyxanalysis
  component "==nyx-store\n<size:16>[Container: Rust library]</size>\n\nWorkspace, workflow, experiment and run storage: manifests, append-only run log, versions, search, .nyx archives. Knows nothing of a project." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsTGlicmFyeQ==>> as nyx.nyxstore
  component "==femcore\n<size:16>[Container: Rust library]</size>\n\nThe FEM core: meshes, meshing and adaptation, linear algebra behind one driver, finite-element basics, the material specification and library, expressions." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsTGlicmFyeQ==>> as nyx.femcore
}

